<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Heleuma — Anchor

//Heleuma//: a stone or iron anchor used to secure a ship.

A ''heleuma'' names any artifact that MUST exist outside the `lar:///` URI space — compiled TypeScript, runtime imperative registrations, build-generated assets — but that ALSO exists inside the meme graph as a self-documenting pair:

* An ''API meme'' (`/api/...`) carrying the contract, the thresholds, and a ''window'' — a `<$transclude>` in its `#source` slot facing the code-file tiddler `module-ref` names. This names the graph's claim on the artifact: it names it, holds its invariants, and marks the precise boundary of what cannot move. The window shows the code where the code-file tiddler stands (shipped by the plugin, or ingested through the TW5 filetype registry); where none stands yet, the window names the seat and stays dark — which reads honestly, since the code living outside the wiki carries the whole reason a heleuma exists.
* A ''doc meme'' (`/docs/...`) carrying the design rationale, the "why it stays stuck here," and the path toward eventual promotion.

A heleuma does not mark failure. It marks a ''named threshold crossing'' — the meme graph asserting sovereignty over something that must, for now, be born outside.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect compiled artifact — TypeScript module, runtime registration, or build asset outside lar:/// space
⏿ orient heleuma tier: ha (permanent structure), ka (promotion-eligible soul/fire), ba (path marker)
◇ ha → no promotion fields; ka → declare source-symbol; body-sha256 optional (keyhive proof is layer 3, planned); ba → the window suffices for reconstruction
▶ pair artifact with API meme + doc meme; declare module-ref; the #source slot transcludes the code-file tiddler; sync-heleuma.ts checks window integrity + module body-sha256
↺ meme graph holds the rope; the artifact holds the anchor; drift surfaces as build warning; confirm heleuma pair complete; drift check registered; promotion path declared or ruled inapplicable

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Heleuma Law (SHALL)

# Every compiled-in artifact that cannot be a first-class `lar:` meme SHALL have a heleuma pair.
# The API meme SHALL declare `heleuma = "ha"`, `"ka"`, or `"ba"` and a `module-ref` naming the code-file tiddler in `#meta`; its `#source` slot SHALL hold a `<$transclude>` window facing `module-ref` and SHALL NOT copy the source. ''One home for the code'': a copy makes two, and two homes for one source drift apart while every check between them chases the gap.
# ''ha'' — body/structure: permanent territory; it declares no `body-sha256`.
# ''ka'' — soul/fire: promotion-eligible. SHALL declare `source-symbol`. MAY declare `body-sha256` (gate layer 2 — content integrity). Keyhive capability proof marks gate layer 3 (planned; not yet implemented).
# ''ba'' — psyche/path: quine-only path marker. `#source` slot sufficient for reconstruction. MAY declare `source-symbol` when a clear symbol boundary exists. When `source-symbol` is declared, MAY declare `body-sha256` for build-time drift detection. A `body-sha256` SHALL accompany a declared `source-symbol`.
# The doc meme SHALL explain why the artifact cannot be promoted and what preconditions would allow promotion (ka) or why promotion is not applicable (ha, ba).
# The build script `sync-heleuma.ts` SHALL verify window integrity (module-ref declared · window standing · window facing the ref) for every mode, and SHALL check drift where drift can live — between the code-file tiddler's body and the live TS (`--sync-modules`, body-sha256). A window cannot drift; only a home can. Findings MUST surface as build warnings; staleness does not block the build but MUST stay visible.
# A code file MAY enter the wiki as a code-file tiddler through the TW5 filetype registry (a `.meta`-paired ingest titles it at its `module-ref` URI), lighting its windows; a standalone module MAY additionally compile TS → CJS through the plugin's own Vite pass and land executable (`application/javascript` + `module-type`). The gate on execution stays import topology — a module whose imports resolve inside the wiki's module space promotes; a barrel spanning files does not.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/freyja-alignment>>

!! Freyja Alignment

Freyja's "Reality Anchor" principle: in a local-first, island-topology system, an anchor functions as the mechanism that lets local changes earn trust and reference across the distributed sea. The heleuma carries the same role in the meme graph — it holds a fixed, named reference point for code that lives in the compiled world, so the graph never encounters surprise from what exists outside it.

The heleuma does not try to absorb the anchor into the graph. It holds the rope.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/promotion-path>>

!! Promotion Path

A heleuma API meme that acquires:

* `confidence ≥ 16`, `mana ≥ 16`, `manao ≥ 16`, `manaoio ≥ 15`
* A verified `body-sha256` hash (gate layer 2 — content integrity; written by `sync-heleuma --commit`)
* A keyhive capability proof (gate layer 3 — operator authorization; planned)

...MAY load through `_bootModules()` via the corpus gate and replace its compiled-in counterpart. At that point the heleuma pair functions as a standard meme pair and `heleuma = true` MAY be removed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

